---
layout: base.njk
bodyClass: home
scripts: ["/assets/js/site.js"]
---
{%- set riskWords = ["", "Low", "Medium", "High"] %}
{%- set famWords = ["", "Unfamiliar", "Partly familiar", "Familiar"] %}
{%- set sizeWords = ["", "Small", "Medium", "Large"] %}
{%- macro meter(label, level, words) %}
<div class="meter" data-level="{{ level }}">
  <dt>{{ label }}</dt>
  <dd><span class="ticks" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span> {{ words[level] }}</dd>
</div>
{%- endmacro %}

<section class="hero" id="compass">
  <div class="wrap hero-grid">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="product"><img src="/assets/compass-mark.png" width="28" height="28" alt=""> Compass, from ayeo</p>
      <h1>Enough process for the work at hand. No&nbsp;more.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Compass is an open-source plugin for <a href="https://claude.com/product/claude-code">Claude Code</a>. It assesses each change by risk, familiarity, size and goal, then sets the process to match: what to write, what to check, and when to ask a human.</p>
      <p class="actions">
        <a class="button" href="#install">Install Compass</a>
        <a class="button quiet" href="{{ site.compass.url }}">Read the code on GitHub</a>
      </p>
      <p class="for-teams">Leading a team? <a href="#teams">See what your team controls</a></p>
    </div>

    {#- The tab roles are added by site.js. Without JavaScript the buttons are
        hidden and every example shows, each under its own heading. #}
    <div class="instrument" data-assessor>
      <p class="instrument-q" id="assessor-q">Pick a change to see how Compass would handle it</p>
      <div class="choices">
        {%- for a in assessments %}
        <button type="button" id="tab-{{ a.id }}" aria-controls="panel-{{ a.id }}">{{ a.change }}</button>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>
      <div class="readouts">
        {%- for a in assessments %}
        <div class="readout" id="panel-{{ a.id }}" {% if not loop.first %}data-hidden{% endif %}>
          <h2 class="prompt"><span aria-hidden="true">&gt;</span> /compass:assess "{{ a.change }}"</h2>
          <dl class="assessment">
            {{ meter("Risk", a.risk, riskWords) }}
            {{ meter("Familiarity", a.familiarity, famWords) }}
            {{ meter("Size", a.size, sizeWords) }}
            <div class="meter goal"><dt>Goal</dt><dd>{{ a.goal }}</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <div class="approach">
            <p class="approach-name">{{ a.approach }}</p>
            <p>{{ a.summary }}</p>
          </div>
          <dl class="plan">
            <div><dt>Writes</dt><dd><ul>{% for w in a.writes %}<li>{{ w }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul></dd></div>
            <div><dt>Checks</dt><dd><ul>{% for c in a.checks %}<li>{{ c }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul></dd></div>
            <div><dt>Asks you</dt><dd>{{ a.asks }}</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Agents in parallel</dt><dd>{{ a.agents }}</dd></div>
            <div class="omitted"><dt>Leaves out, and says why</dt><dd>{{ a.leavesOut }}</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </div>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>
      <p class="instrument-note">Illustrative. In your project, the <a href="#teams">routing policy</a> makes the call.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band" id="install">
  <div class="wrap two-col">
    <div>
      <h2>Install it in Claude Code</h2>
      <p>Run these two commands inside Claude Code. You need Python 3.10 or later. The default guardrails work straight away; project setup is optional.</p>
      <p>Compass does nothing in a repository until someone runs a Compass command there. It works on your machine and reaches the network only when you ask it to.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="code-stack">
      <div class="code"><code>/plugin marketplace add {{ site.compass.repo }}</code><button type="button" class="copy" data-copy="/plugin marketplace add {{ site.compass.repo }}">Copy</button></div>
      <div class="code"><code>/plugin install compass@compass</code><button type="button" class="copy" data-copy="/plugin install compass@compass">Copy</button></div>
      <p class="code-after">Then describe the work:</p>
      <div class="code"><code>/compass:assess "Add rate limiting to the public API"</code><button type="button" class="copy" data-copy='/compass:assess "Add rate limiting to the public API"'>Copy</button></div>
      <p class="small">Prefer source? <a href="{{ site.compass.url }}#start-here">Clone and install from GitHub</a>. Compass sits alongside your CI. It doesn't replace your tests, linting or security scanning.</p>
      <p class="visually-hidden" aria-live="polite" data-copy-status></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="prose-block">
      <h2>You don't pick the process. The work does.</h2>
      <p>A typo fix shouldn't need an architecture pack. A payments rewrite shouldn't start from an unstructured prompt. Most spec-driven setups give you one workflow for everything, or leave you to choose one each time.</p>
      <p>Compass puts the judgement in one place: the assessment. Everything after it is deterministic. The same assessment under the same policy gives the same approach, every time, so you can see why a change got the process it did and argue with the policy rather than the agent.</p>
    </div>

    <figure class="pipeline">
      <ol>
        <li>assess</li><li>define</li><li>plan</li><li>implement</li><li>verify</li><li>ship</li>
      </ol>
      <figcaption>Every change goes through the same six stages. How deep each one goes is what changes.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section tinted" id="teams">
  <div class="wrap two-col">
    <div>
      <h2>What your team controls</h2>
      <p>The rules live in one file in each repository, <code>compass.yml</code>, which you review like any other code.</p>
      <dl class="controls">
        <div>
          <dt>Who signs off</dt>
          <dd>A person must approve auth and access changes, payments, personal data, migrations and anything that could lose data or resist rollback. The record names the approver, their role, the decision, the time and the scope.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>One policy across repositories</dt>
          <dd>Each repository can extend a shared policy, pinned to an exact commit. <code>compass policy diff</code> shows whether a change to it tightens or loosens the rules.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Whether checks block</dt>
          <dd>With <code>adoption: enforced</code>, a failed check fails <code>compass check</code> and CI. Use <code>advisory</code> to pilot Compass without blocking delivery.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>How often agents stop</dt>
          <dd><code>autonomy</code> sets whether a session waits for a person at every hand-off, some of them, or none.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
      <p class="small">Compass governs its own workflow, not every agent action. Keep branch protection, code review and CI. Read the <a href="https://docs.ayeo.io/compass/safety-contract/">safety contract</a> and the <a href="https://docs.ayeo.io/compass/configuration/">configuration guide</a>.</p>
    </div>
    <pre class="tree policy" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Example compass.yml"><code><span># compass.yml (example)</span>
schema: 1

<span># Share one policy, pinned to a commit</span>
extends: github:acme/compass-banking@1.2.0#3f9c1a2e…

<span># Approves waivers and confirms agents' decisions</span>
owner: tech-lead

<span># A failed check fails CI</span>
adoption: enforced

<span># Wait for a person at every hand-off</span>
autonomy: controlled</code></pre>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Rigour without ritual</h2>
    <div class="rules">
      <div>
        <h3>Guardrails</h3>
        <p>Few, checkable and blocking. The CLI enforces them.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Tested before it ships</li>
          <li>Acceptance defined before implementation</li>
          <li>Every change traced to what asked for it</li>
          <li>Evidence, not assertion</li>
          <li>A person approves anything irreversible</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Strategies</h3>
        <p>Strong defaults that apply when they add value, and step aside when they don't.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Behaviour specs as Given/When/Then scenarios</li>
          <li>Test-driven development</li>
          <li>Architecture decision records and diagrams</li>
          <li>Parallel agents, each in its own git worktree</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section tinted">
  <div class="wrap two-col">
    <div>
      <h2>Every change leaves a record</h2>
      <p>Each issue gets a folder you can review and resume from, without relying on chat history. It shows the current decision, what needs your approval, the approach Compass chose, what it left out and why, and the evidence behind each stage.</p>
      <p>Another session, or another person, can pick it up from there.</p>
    </div>
    <pre class="tree" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Example record folder"><code>.compass/work/rate-limiting/
├── dashboard        <span>current decision, what needs approval</span>
├── approach         <span>what was chosen, and what was left out</span>
├── spec.feature     <span>the behaviour, as scenarios</span>
├── design           <span>proportionate to the risk</span>
└── evidence/        <span>test runs, approvals and checks</span></code></pre>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Open and portable</h2>
    <p class="narrow">Compass is open source under the {{ site.compass.licence }} licence. It runs on Claude Code today, and its core doesn't depend on it.</p>
    <dl class="layers">
      <div><dt>Methodology</dt><dd>The guidance, governance and templates, in plain language.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Kit</dt><dd>The Python command-line tool and policy engine. It doesn't depend on Claude Code.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Adapter</dt><dd>The Claude Code plugin: commands, agents, skills and hooks. An adapter for another tool would reuse the kit.</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

{%- set latest = collections.news | head(3) %}
<section class="section tinted" id="news">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>What we plan to build</h2>
      {%- if latest.length %}<a href="/news/">All news</a>{% endif %}
    </div>
    <p class="narrow">Before we build anything, we write the announcement and the FAQ as if it had already shipped. When we commit to one, it goes up here with its status, so you can see what's coming and tell us early if we've got it wrong.</p>
    {%- if latest.length %}
    <ul class="news-list">
      {%- for post in latest %}
      {% include "news-item.njk" %}
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
    {%- else %}
    <p>Nothing published yet. <a href="/news/feed.xml">Follow the feed</a> to hear about the first one.</p>
    {%- endif %}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band closing">
  <div class="wrap closing-inner">
    <h2>Try it on your next change</h2>
    <p class="actions">
      <a class="button" href="#install">Install Compass</a>
      <a class="button quiet" href="https://docs.ayeo.io/compass/">Read the docs</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
